      "card_ids": ["C02","C08","C10","C12","C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 aprepitant records show 10 mg/mL solubility in a self-emulsifying vehicle and increased dissolution rate for an optimized self-emulsifying formulation, consistent with the high human F values and indicating that low aqueous solubility is not an inherent barrier for this structural class when formulated.",
      "card_ids": ["C51","C53"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 torcetrapib and phenobarbital records are formulation solubility/dissolution data in lipid vehicles or salt forms; they do not measure permeability or absolute F for the query and provide no affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C49","C50","C52","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 low rat F values for silodosin (9.2%) and bitopertin (14–23%) are species/formulation-specific and do not overturn the human high-F direction.",
